-- title:
--   Normal two-dimensional stalk at a non-crossing rational point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and the hypothesis `hj` that `jqModC ℚ` lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}$-Laurent series. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the curve $X$ of level `ΓM M H` over `R p`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R p \to A$ lift the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O'$ be a discrete valuation domain with a map $\rho_{O'} : R p \to O'$, an injective local injection $\iota : O' \to A$ with $\iota \circ \rho_{O'} = \rho$, a map $j_{O'} : O' \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with $\rho_{O'}$ and with the inclusion of $A$, compatibility of the induced maps to $\kappa$, and a generator $\varpi'$ of the maximal ideal of $O'$. Let $u_\kappa$ be a $\kappa$-point of the fibre of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` over $\kappa$, that is, a section of the second projection, and suppose for some $i \in \{0,1\}$ that the image of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ under $u_\kappa$ avoids the image of the $i$-th component map $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}$. Put $X_{O'} =$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO'`, the base change of the model along $\rho_{O'}$, let $x'$ be the image of that closed point under the base-change map `bcMap` attached to the residue map $O' \to \kappa$, let $B$ be the stalk of $X_{O'}$ at $x'$, and let $\sigma_B : O' \to B$ be the structural map obtained from the germ at $x'$ of the pullback of global sections along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O'$. Then, assuming the residue field map of that structure morphism at $x'$ is an isomorphism, $B$ is a noetherian integrally closed domain with $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} B = 2$, and the ideal $\sigma_B(\varpi')B$ is prime. The statement also names the generic-fibre pullback over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the projection from it to $X_{O'}$ induced by $j_{O'}$; neither occurs in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the local statement that the Deligne–Rapoport style model of $X_H$, base changed to a coefficient discrete valuation ring $O'$ inside $A$, has a two-dimensional normal noetherian local ring at a point of the special fibre lying off one of the two components, with the vertical ideal generated by a uniformiser prime; the rationality hypothesis on the residue field at $x'$ makes the special fibre there the spectrum of a discrete valuation ring. It feeds the Hartogs-type descent arguments that read sections of the model at such points and compare them with integral $q$-expansions.
